            <ArticleTitle>Quality measurement issues in heart disease in women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>241-8; discussion 248-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heart disease in women has evolved to an acknowledged set of conditions, with standards and valid recommendations. The quality of care for women at risk for heart disease now can be assessed to improve health outcomes. The knowledge base for quality assessment in heart disease in women is addressed with respect to coronary heart disease risk factors, treatment disparities, and diagnostic testing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
